  "question": {
    "text": "The values of $a, b, c$ for which the function $f(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}\\frac{\\sin (a+1) x+\\sin x}{x}, x < 0 \\\\ c, x=0 \\\\ \\frac{\\left(x+b x^2\\right)^{1 / 2}-\\sqrt{x}}{b x^{1 / 2}}, x>0\\end{array}\\right.$ is continuous at $x=0$, are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iKQLi",
      "text": "$a=\\frac{3}{2}, b=-\\frac{3}{2}, c=\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "J3bG7",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{a}=-\\frac{3}{2}, \\mathrm{c}=\\frac{3}{2}, \\mathrm{~b}$ is arbitrary non-zero real number",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dhkk5",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{a}=-\\frac{5}{2}, \\mathrm{~b}=-\\frac{3}{2}, \\mathrm{c}=\\frac{3}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hu1a0",
      "text": "$a=-2, b \\in \\mathbb{R}-\\{0\\}, c=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad f\\left(0^{+}\\right)=\\underset{x \\rightarrow 0^{+}}{L t} \\frac{(1+b x)^{1 / 2}-1}{b}=0$\n$f(0)=c$\n$f\\left(0^{-}\\right)=a+2$\n$\\Rightarrow c=0$ and $a=-2, b \\in R-\\{0\\}$",
